ems are and  based on that I'll be able to tailor the  discussion to be able to help them solve  their problems right if they have a  strong pain point and you're able to  help solve that you're much more likely  to get the sale so what I'll do is I'll  always ask about the challenges they're  facing and for every person I meet it  could be a different child  so it could be having problems with a  business partner or trying to raise  capital or trying to grow their business  and get more sales and marketing  whatever it is is a different challenge  for every person and so I don't make  sure I know what their main points are  before us are talking about what I have  to offer so we'll spend some time  talking about their business that pain  points they're having and then once  you've had any discussion around that  I'll say well let me tell you a little  bit more about our service and you can  see if it's a fit for you or not and  answer any questions hopeful that you  have and usually then you'll say yes  it's great let's learn more and again  I'm getting their body so you want to  make sure that it's not just a sales  presentation that at the end they say  yes or no to but they have an active  role in the entire discussion so it  starts off with them talking about it  and people love talking about themselves  and so that gets them a little bit more  invested too into your potential product  or service and hopefully close in a sale  and then by learning more about them  you're able to tailor your presentation  to be able to fit the particular or  sales problems that they're happening at  their company so I hope that helps  that's a little bit of how I will first  get introduced to a client and start the  sales process if you have extra  questions you know let me know in the  comments below I'd also love if you can  give it a thumbs up and stay tuned for  the next episode  you
 

